<title>USA: U.S. 3-, 6-month auction seen at 5.08-9, 5.12 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. 3-, 6-month auction seen at 5.08-9, 5.12 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury's sale of $16.0 billion in three- and six months bills was expected to produce average discount rates of 5.08-5.09 and 5.12 percent, respectively, traders said.</p>
<p>In when-issued trading at 1240 EDT/1640 GMT, the three-month bill was at 5.11 percent and the six-month bill was at 5.12 percent.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
